To convert a number such as
\[x=(\xi)_{(10)}\cdot 10^{k}\]

to the binary scale, where k is a positive integer so large that Table28.1 cannot be used, apply the following device: Compute

\[\log_2x=\frac{\log_10x}{\log_10x}2=k+\frac{x_1}{\log_102}2\]

where k is the quotient and x_1 the remainder, the division being carried out in the decimal scale. Then find n=10^n, i.e., x_1=\log_10^n, so that \cdot

\[\log_2x=k+\frac{\log_10^n}{\log_10x}2=k+\log_2^n whenever x=(n)_{(10)}2^k.\]

Now convert (n)_{(10)} to the binary scale by any of the methods described above.

A similar device may be used to convert to the decimal scale a binary number that is outside the range of Table28.1.

